        <p>I'm a UX designer who comes from sales, running a business, and astrophysics research. I spent seven years owning client accounts and leading sales teams, and I ran my own sports bar and grill. Those jobs taught me that most products fail at the point where a real person gets stuck.</p>
        <p>That's why I started <a href="/design/rinkside-b2c/">Rinkside</a>. Booking a drop-in skate at a Denver rink took me 13 taps across 3 websites, so I researched it, designed a one-app fix, and built a working alpha with Claude Code. Now I'm working on the <a href="/design/rinkside-b2b/">rink-staff side</a> of it.</p>
        <p>I like owning a product end to end: research, design, and build. I'm looking for an entry-level UX role at a startup or mid-size company where I can do all three.</p>
